### ============================================================
### TC-P03 — Auth: Recuperación y Restablecimiento de Password
### ============================================================
### Flujo: solicitar recuperación → obtener token de la DB →
### restablecer → login con nueva password.
### Requiere: usuario registrado y verificado (TC-P01).
### ============================================================

### ── Solicitar recuperación ──────────────────────────────────

### TC-P03-01 — Recuperar password John (email existe) → 202
# Después de esto consultar la DB para obtener el token:
#   SELECT valor FROM token_usuario
#   WHERE tipo='RESET_PASSWORD' AND consumido_en IS NULL
#   ORDER BY id DESC LIMIT 1;
# @name u1_recuperar
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/recuperar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{u1Email}}"
}

### TC-P03-02 — Recuperar password (email no existe) → 202
# Anti-enumeración: siempre 202, no revela si el email existe
# @name recuperar_email_inexistente
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/recuperar
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "fantasma@uce.edu.ec"
}

### ── Restablecer password ────────────────────────────────────

### TC-P03-03 — Token inválido → 410
# @name restablecer_token_invalido
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/restablecer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "token-que-no-existe-abc123",
  "password": "NuevaClave123",
  "passwordConfirmacion": "NuevaClave123"
}

### TC-P03-04 — Passwords no coinciden → 400
# Reemplazar {{u1_token_reset}} con el token de la DB
# @name restablecer_passwords_no_coinciden
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/restablecer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{u1_token_reset}}",
  "password": "{{u1PasswordNueva}}",
  "passwordConfirmacion": "OtraClave999"
}

### TC-P03-05 — Password nueva no cumple política → 400
# @name restablecer_password_debil
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/restablecer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{u1_token_reset}}",
  "password": "corta",
  "passwordConfirmacion": "corta"
}

### TC-P03-06 — Restablecer exitoso → 204
# Reemplazar {{u1_token_reset}} con el token real de la DB
# D-03: después de esto TODOS los refresh tokens quedan revocados
# @name restablecer_exitoso
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/restablecer
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "token": "{{u1_token_reset}}",
  "password": "{{u1PasswordNueva}}",
  "passwordConfirmacion": "{{u1PasswordNueva}}"
}

### ── Verificar cambio ────────────────────────────────────────

### TC-P03-07 — Login con password vieja → 401
# Ya no debería funcionar
# @name u1_login_password_vieja
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{u1Email}}",
  "password": "{{u1Password}}",
  "recordarSesion": true
}

### TC-P03-08 — Login con password nueva → 200
# @name u1_login_password_nueva
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "{{u1Email}}",
  "password": "{{u1PasswordNueva}}",
  "recordarSesion": true
}

> {%
  client.global.set("u1_access_token", response.body.accessToken);
  client.global.set("u1_refresh_token", response.body.refreshToken);
%}
